WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.109 --> 00:00:05.649
Hey youtubers it’s charlie and lots of Arrow
stuff to talk about. We got a new trailer

00:00:05.649 --> 00:00:10.839
with Ra’s Al Ghul that I’ll breakdown
and a couple big new cast members in the last

00:00:10.839 --> 00:00:11.230
week. Most notably Ra’s Al Ghul but just
as I was writing this they announced JR Ramirez

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:14.839
as the Ted Grant Wildcat. I’ll mention him
briefly but mostly this video will just be

00:00:14.839 --> 00:00:21.839
about the trailer. I’ll do a separate video
just for Wildcat.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:26.920
Hello new people, if you’re just now finding
me or you found me during Comic Con I do Arrow

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:31.200
and Flash videos every week. Be sure to subscribe
to get everything. At the end of this video

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.969
I’ll announce the winner of the giveaway.

00:00:32.969 --> 00:00:36.620
So let’s rip that trailer apart. Frame for
frame. Right of the bat you see the brand

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:43.620
new motion logo Warner Brothers made for Arrow.
They made a red flash one and a rainy depressing

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:48.390
looking one for Gotham. It’s like they uploaded
a custom banner for each new DC TV Show. I

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:52.630
didn’t see a Constantine one, but they just
might not have released it yet.

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:58.250
The opening voice over where Oliver is looking
out over the city is a line from Huntress

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:04.629
last season. I almost thought it was Thea,
but really the first half of the trailer is

00:01:04.629 --> 00:01:10.420
a recap of Season 2, so everything is taken
from those episodes. So the line is clipped

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:13.549
directly from the Birds of Prey episode.

00:01:13.549 --> 00:01:18.020
We see all the big WTF action scenes and the
progression of Deathstroke’s plan to crush

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:23.340
Oliver into darkness by Killing Moira, everyone
and everything he loves. This is the first

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.810
promo of the season, so a lot of this is just
to help new people catch up with the plot.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:30.729
What really ended up happening and what Oliver
says in that final line to Slade is that all

00:01:30.729 --> 00:01:34.409
that crazy shit galvanized him into a hero.
So in episode 1 of season 3. Oliver is full

00:01:34.409 --> 00:01:37.450
on embracing his role as a hero of the city.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:40.560
Here’s where we start seeing new footage.
The opening line is from the new character

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:45.740
Maseo Yamashiro, played by Karl Yune. He’s
going to be Oliver’s Diggle in the Hong

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:52.740
Kong Flashbacks. His wife is Katana. Although
in the past she might not have taken up that

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:58.170
name yet. In the comics, she only becomes
Katana after her husband is murdered. So we’ll

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:01.689
have to see how closely Arrow is sticking
to the comics.

00:02:01.689 --> 00:02:06.310
What he’s talking about when he says a man
can’t live by two names. He’s just talking

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:11.830
about secret identities and alter egos. In
the flashbacks, Oliver still hasn’t become

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:14.950
the hero. So part of his journey is going
to be learning who he really is. Is he Oliver

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:18.500
Queen billionaire or is he going to try and
be a force for justice.

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:21.260
The context they’re speaking in is a little
weird. Katana and her husband are going to

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:27.410
be Oliver’s Hong Kong handlers. They work
for Amanda Waller. Probably not by choice,

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:33.739
but Oliver is forced to work for her too.
So together, the three of them will try to

00:02:33.739 --> 00:02:37.190
make the best of a bad situation and learn
how to serve justice while still being under

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:40.959
the thumb of ARGUS.
Like learning to be the better man despite

00:02:40.959 --> 00:02:43.450
circumstances telling him his job is to be
Waller’s hitman.

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:50.450
Then we see Oliver addressing what’s left
of Queen Industries after Slade and Isobel’s

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:56.750
influence have been purged. I’m not sure
if she ran it into the ground or just pushed

00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:00.840
Oliver out. I’ll explain more about that
in a sec when we see Brandon Routh.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:05.830
This blue looking scene is connected to the
new medium bad Werner Zyrtle also called Count

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:10.300
Vertigo played by Peter Stormare. It’s probably
his lab where he manufactures the Vertigo

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.080
drug.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:18.080
Here where Laurel says she and Oliver are
business partners it kind of ties in directly

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:23.560
with the next scene but Laurel helps Oliver
get the funds to buy back his company. Thus

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:28.200
she becomes his business partner. But wait,
in this next scene Ray Palmer also known as

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:33.569
The Atom swoops in or shrinks in I should
say. Brandon Routh is essentially buying a

00:03:33.569 --> 00:03:39.319
controlling interest in Oliver’s company.
Making him Oliver’s new boss.

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:46.319
This isn’t a bad thing, because the Atom
is another Justice League member who will

00:03:51.209 --> 00:03:56.470
eventually join team Arrow. It’s just that
when they first meet it’s super awkward.

00:03:56.470 --> 00:04:01.069
Plus he’s going to compete with Oliver for
Felicity’s affections. I know a lot of you

00:04:01.069 --> 00:04:06.680
Olicity shippers will grind your teeth, but
Brandon Routh is a cool dude so this is going

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:12.599
to be fun.

00:04:12.599 --> 00:04:16.379
Ray Palmer’s business relationship with
Oliver will of course over time turn into

00:04:16.379 --> 00:04:21.009
a night time vigilante relationship. That’s
one of the major arcs of the season. The evolution

00:04:21.009 --> 00:04:23.339
of Ray Palmer into the Atom.

00:04:23.339 --> 00:04:30.339
Then Oliver is explaining to Diggle that because
he’s got a mini Diggle he can’t keep putting

00:04:33.229 --> 00:04:38.139
himself in danger. Diggle and Lyla’s baby
will be another big arc for David Ramsey.

00:04:38.139 --> 00:04:41.909
Diggle balancing fatherhood with night time
activities. I know everyone wanted to see

00:04:41.909 --> 00:04:48.909
a Connor Hawke arc with Oliver, but it seems
like they’re giving that to Diggle’s character.

00:04:55.669 --> 00:05:00.699
Here’s the first look of Peter Stormare
as Count Vertigo. I don’t know if he’s

00:05:00.699 --> 00:05:04.509
going to call himself that or if it will just
be an affectation that other people attach

00:05:04.509 --> 00:05:07.719
to him because of all the Vertigo he sells.
His real name is Werner Zytle.

00:05:07.719 --> 00:05:12.879
I think that when he’s talking about Oliver
refusing to die, he’s talking about the

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:19.089
big attack during the first episode as well
as season 2 with Slade. It seems like Count

00:05:19.089 --> 00:05:22.830
Vertigo has history with Starling City. Like
he watched all the crap go on last season

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:29.649
and waited for his moment to jump in and start
pushing Vertigo Drugs again.

00:05:29.649 --> 00:05:36.649
Here’s Black Canary, back in black leather
kicking butt. They announced she was coming

00:05:38.819 --> 00:05:41.619
back so this isn’t a surprise. But it’s
hard to tell who’s ass she’s kicking.

00:05:41.619 --> 00:05:46.330
It looks like it might be Sin and the guy
she was beating up might have been trying

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:50.789
to hurt her. They way they edited it is a
little confusing. This hoodie person is not

00:05:50.789 --> 00:05:56.960
the person she just took down.
Her next scene is one from last season, the

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:02.509
episode where she took off. It’s teeing
up the Olicity arc that’s going to be a

00:06:02.509 --> 00:06:06.409
big deal this year. When I say Olicity, I’m
just talking about the show dealing with the

00:06:06.409 --> 00:06:11.819
sexual tension in a more literal context.

00:06:11.819 --> 00:06:18.819
Cut to said proposal and then said date. Stephen
Amell was asked at comic con how their date

00:06:18.849 --> 00:06:23.149
would go and he laughed and said “Horribly”.
You’ll see why in a sec. But their conversation.

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:30.149
It’s about Oliver explaining his time in
Hong Kong.

00:06:31.429 --> 00:06:37.589
Cut to Hong Kong parkour. I believe this person
is Karl Yune again. Probably when he and Oliver

00:06:37.589 --> 00:06:40.379
first meet. He’s not just his handler and
his friend. He’s also going to continue

00:06:40.379 --> 00:06:47.379
Oliver’s training along with Katana. It
doesn’t start out as a very happy partnership.

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:54.449
The next scene kind of explains all that Hong
Kong craziness in the earlier scene. Oliver

00:06:54.449 --> 00:07:00.149
is trying to escape Hong Kong and Waller is
keeping him there to serve her purpose. I

00:07:00.149 --> 00:07:04.419
love how there’s Green Cloth covering the
windows. Foreshadowing much?

00:07:04.419 --> 00:07:07.610
This is just another scene from him trying
to escape. That parkour fight with Maseo.

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:11.709
Cut to rooftop reveal of Oliver on the same
roof where we saw Caity Lotz. I’m guessing

00:07:11.709 --> 00:07:16.679
they’re taking out someone in that first
episode. Most of the footage in these are

00:07:16.679 --> 00:07:18.659
from the first couple of episodes only.

00:07:18.659 --> 00:07:22.860
But then we see Roy in his new costume. He’s
the Arsenal version of Roy Harper. Stephen

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:27.439
Amell joked that he now had the second best
costume on the show. Just because Colton’s

00:07:27.439 --> 00:07:33.289
looks so cool. He’s right, Roy’s costume
is way better than Olivers.

00:07:33.289 --> 00:07:40.289
Quentin here is in his captain’s uniform
with a shaved head and a hat. This is his

00:07:47.879 --> 00:07:52.659
costume for season 3, so to speak. Paul Blackthorne
looks a little strange at first with a shaved

00:07:52.659 --> 00:07:57.099
head. But I like it. The bright light they
have him framed in here pretty much tells

00:07:57.099 --> 00:07:59.459
you he’s riding high.

00:07:59.459 --> 00:08:04.649
He’s in a position of power and able to
use the police force to help Team Arrow take

00:08:04.649 --> 00:08:05.969
down bad guys.

00:08:05.969 --> 00:08:10.509
WTF is this? Star City? I know a lot of you
comic book fans will get excited about this.

00:08:10.509 --> 00:08:15.360
In the comics. Star City is the name of Oliver
Queen’s home. Starling city is just something

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:16.489
Arrow changed.

00:08:16.489 --> 00:08:23.489
It looks like Ray Palmer is going to try and
rejuvenate and re-brand the entire city. Which

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:29.779
seems kind of strange at first. Think of Starling
City as an analog of Coast City. The one that

00:08:29.779 --> 00:08:36.779
was destroyed during Reign of the Supermen.
Hank Henshaw, the cyborg superman wiped it

00:08:37.319 --> 00:08:40.919
off the face of the map. But eventually with
the help of the earth’s super heroes and

00:08:40.919 --> 00:08:46.860
the green lantern corps, the city was rebuilt
as the “City Without Fear”. That was also

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:52.139
a tie in to the Sinestro Corps war storyline.
Which was also a Geoff Johns written story.

00:08:52.139 --> 00:08:58.170
I love how you see his fingerprints over all
these elements of Arrow.

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:05.170
Ray Palmer on Arrow is going to be a tech
genius, so whatever his plan for revitalizing

00:09:06.139 --> 00:09:08.230
Starling City is, it will be tech based.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:13.699
This fandom heart attack is what happens after
the Olicity date in that first episode. So

00:09:13.699 --> 00:09:16.680
now you understand why Stephen Amell said
their date goes horribly. She’s obviously

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:22.180
going to recover. But this is the event that
shocks Oliver awake. He’s kind of been “coasting”

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:26.740
in the months of vacation time since Slade
was stuck in that ARGUS prison.

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:30.269
I know everyone was excited to hear him say
the line again. You Have Failed this City.

00:09:30.269 --> 00:09:34.709
We don’t see who he’s saying it to, but
usually when he says that to someone it’s

00:09:34.709 --> 00:09:40.430
a person with deep roots in Starling. Which
I’m guessing is not Count Vertigo. It might

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:44.940
be Merlyn he’s talking to, but we don’t
know when he’ll make his first season 3

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:50.560
appearance. He’s a cast regular. So I’m
hoping he’s in that first episode.

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:54.410
And then there’s the icing on the cake.
The Ra’s Al Ghul scene. It’s just a teaser,

00:09:54.410 --> 00:09:59.329
the reason we don’t see his face is because
they haven’t cast the role yet. Or if they

00:09:59.329 --> 00:10:01.569
found someone, they haven’t announced who
it is.

00:10:01.569 --> 00:10:05.220
I can’t remember when I started predicting
Ra’s Al Ghul because we all expected him

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:12.220
to be in the finale last year. Like as a post
credits teaser. I’m not surprised that Arrow

00:10:15.879 --> 00:10:21.050
is bringing him on, but I am surprised that
they full on announced it. Usually things

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:22.579
like this they keep secret until the episodes
air.

00:10:22.579 --> 00:10:27.199
Other than wanting to kill Merlyn, there are
only a few reasons he would bring himself

00:10:27.199 --> 00:10:31.500
to Starling. I would say it has something
to do with Waller’s actions in the Hong

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:34.290
Kong flashbacks and Count Vertigo in the present.

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:36.970
We have all these new characters, and by the
season 3 finale. All of their stories have

00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:40.680
to intersect in the present. So I’ll be
interested to see how the dots are connected

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:47.399
from Oliver to Amanda Waller to Katana to
Ra’s Al Ghul to Merlyn to Ray Palmer.

00:10:47.399 --> 00:10:54.399
And that doesn’t even cover the Flash crossover.
I’m interested to see how the Flash characters

00:10:55.149 --> 00:10:59.439
overlap with the new Arrow characters or if
it’s going to be a one of special self contained

00:10:59.439 --> 00:11:03.310
plot. It sounds like based on what they’re
saying. The two different parts of it, episode

00:11:03.310 --> 00:11:09.930
8 of both shows. Will tie some big arcs from
each show together. Like the villains on the

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:13.649
flash will overlap with the villains on Arrow
and it will take both sets of superheroes

00:11:13.649 --> 00:11:15.430
coming together to stop them.

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:22.009
Like a mini Justice League episode. Be sure
to let me know what you’re most excited

00:11:22.009 --> 00:11:24.839
about after watching this trailer.

00:11:24.839 --> 00:11:31.839
Now let’s talk about the Ted Grant Wildcat.
JR Ramirez has been cast and it looks like

00:11:32.069 --> 00:11:36.370
they’re going full on with the boxing aspects
of his character. In the comics, Ted Grant

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:40.740
was a prize fighter that started wearing a
costume and kicking bad guys butts. He was

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:44.660
a core member of the Justice Society. And
as you can see here, some recommended reading

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:51.009
for his backstory is Sensation Comics #1,
JSA Classified 8 and 9 and Batman/Wildcat

00:11:51.009 --> 00:11:52.529
1 through 3.

00:11:52.529 --> 00:11:57.350
Geoff Johns had a long run on JSA about 10
years ago, so once again you see his fingerprints

00:11:57.350 --> 00:12:01.290
on Arrow storylines. I’ll be doing a separate
video for him, be sure to subscribe to get

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:01.730
it.

